                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is designed for eight-year clinical medical students.&nbsp;<em>Pediatrics</em>&nbsp;is a medical science that studies the growth and development, healthcare, and disease prevention and treatment in children. It is a compulsory subject for medical students.From the fetal stage to adolescence, children undergo continuous maturation in physical, psychological, and intellectual aspects. Their anatomical, physiological, and pathological characteristics, as well as the occurrence, progression, and management of diseases, differ significantly from those of adults and vary across different age groups.The course covers fundamental knowledge of pediatrics and theoretical concepts of common and frequently encountered pediatric diseases. Beyond professional theoretical knowledge, the course aims to:Deepen professional identity through the spirit of pediatrics；Learn from esteemed medical predecessors to foster lofty ideals；Share pediatric stories to cultivate a sense of national and familial responsibility.The ultimate goal is to cultivate medical professionals who embody both humanistic and scientific spirit, combining compassion with competence.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
